)F FUNCTION -                                                                   
  The CONNECT command connects an existing RAKF user to a new                   
  GROUP.                                                                        
  It adds a new record in SYS1.SECURE.CNTL(USERS) of this user                  
  with a new GROUP.                                                             
                                                                                
  CONNECT updates the control data sets on disk only. Reload the in             
  core tables afterwards with 'S RAKFUSER' from the console, or by              
  running the RAKFUSER procedure in batch.                                      
                                                                                
  You must be connected to the RAKFADM group.  CONNECT is an ordinary           
  problem state program - it is the protection on the control data sets         
  that enforces this, not APF authorization.                                    
)X SYNTAX -                                                                     
  CONNECT userid GROUP(group)                                                   
                                                                                
  REQUIRED - userid                                                             
             GROUP                                                              
                                                                                
  RETURN CODES:                                                                 
                                                                                
     0 - The user is connected to the group.                                    
     8 - An error occurs. A suitable message will be given to                   
         the user.                                                              
                                                                                
  SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS:                                                         
                                                                                
     The issuing user should have the SPECIAL authority.                        
     Update access to the SYS1.SECURE.* dataset is necessary or                 
     the issuing user should have the OPERATIONS authority along                
     with the SPECIAL authority.                                                
                                                                                
)O OPERANDS -                                                                   
))USERID - the user to connect. 1 to 8 characters. Required, and is the         
  first operandd. If the user don't exist, nothing will happen and              
  the user will be notified.                                                    
))GROUP - the group name to which the user will be connected. Required.         
  The group may not exist in user entry in the USERS member.                    
